@techReport{KayaResearch2022,
   abstract = {Private and Confidential 2 Furthermore, the enforcement of the Social and Governance dimensions of ESG are gaining traction in mainstream politics in the US, UK, and EU, which helps to reinforce friendshoring efforts. For example, the possible integration of ESG criteria in tendering processes that prohibit the use of products connected to slave labour or human rights abuses could effectively exclude Chinese bidders unable to meet thresholds. This will also affect Western manufacturers dependent on Chinese components for critical elements of their production. American friendshoring has caused consternation in China, and it remains to be seen how China will react to European leveraging ESG to effectively achieve the same objectives. Security concerns are gaining momentum as global tensions point to a confrontational stance not only between the West (broadly, NATO countries) and Russia, but increasingly between NATO and China. The US intends to use the June NATO summit to engage the Alliance more strongly as a bulwark against rising Chinese strategic influence. While this new containment strategy has a military dimension, it also relates to technology and trade. Figure 1. China produces approximately 50% of the world's metals, 60% of its wind turbines, and 70% of its solar panels, while comprising only 18% of global GDP (Thunder Said Energy). 0% 20% 40% 60% 80% 100% China Market Share Structural Solar Wind},
